type: software
title: "Sharp constants for sums of matrix moduli when 1<p<2"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. For 1<p<2 and n-by-n matrices: the best Schatten-norm constant c_p(m,n) in ||A_1+...+A_m||_p <= c ||(|A_1|+...+|A_m|)||_p equals an explicit one-variable maximum D_{p,n} when m >= n (equality cases classified, strict for m < n; rank-one summands solved in every dimension); c_p(m) <= ((1+sqrt m)/2)^{1-1/p} by log-convexity in 1/p, improving m^{(p-1)/(2p)}; and a computer-assisted proof in exact arithmetic that two 3x3 matrices beat the rank-one value D_{p,2} at nine exponents between 11/10 and 17/10."
